Date: Thu, 25 Jun 2026 06:26:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03961/11362] [outer-loop] graded-goal-bias A/B: fix is correct
 but the wall is UPSTREAM (goal induction), not the bias

Outcome C: the graded path is correctly wired (exemplar captured, env gate works,
win_state_exemplar_injected=True) but never reached _install_goal_bias on lp85 L2 --
the Qwen3.5-9B-MTP proposer returned ok=False/proposer_failed on the L2 reinduction
(generated 2194+ tokens, output failed Python extraction). And BOTH arms show
goal_predicate_satisfiable=False. So the binding constraint for lp85 L2 deepening is
GOAL INDUCTION (the LLM proposer cannot generate a satisfiable L2 world-model/goal for
lp85's alignment mechanic), NOT the frontier bias -- consistent with .430/.434
(goal_predicate_satisfiable=False) and the goal-free probe. The graded-goal-energy fix
(05970b9c6) is a real, parity-safe improvement that removes the binary-cliff
degradation and WILL help once a satisfiable goal is induced, but it is
necessary-but-insufficient: it cannot bank lp85 L2 alone. (sc25 not run -- the live-LLM
2x2 was killed at 244min; lp85 establishes the upstream wall.)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
